{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>His guilt — its principal.</b> That is the principal sum he swore falsely about (Bava Kamma 110a)." "<b>To the one to whom he is guilty.</b> To the one against whom he incurred liability (Ketubot 19a)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "Rashi's Hebrew reads 'שנשבע עליו' — 'that he swore upon.' The Talmudic context (Bava Kamma) concerns a deposit denied under oath; 'its principal' (הקרן) is the deposited sum itself, to which a fifth is added."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:26.482685483Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}